---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — SubHelm';
const description =
  'SubHelm privacy policy. Your subscriptions stay on your device: no account, no ads, no cross-app tracking.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 2 July 2026</p>

    <p>
      SubHelm is built privacy-first. There is no account, no sign-up, and no
      advertising or cross-app tracking. This policy explains exactly what
      happens to your data.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your subscriptions are stored <strong>on your device</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        If you're signed into iCloud, they sync through <strong>your own private
        iCloud account</strong> (Apple CloudKit). We, the developers, <strong>cannot
        see them</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        We do <strong>not</strong> collect, sell, or share your personal data. Your
        subscription names, amounts, and notes never leave your device for our benefit.
      </li>
      <li>
        We use <strong>anonymous, aggregate product analytics</strong> (TelemetryDeck)
        to understand which features are used, never your content, and you can turn
        it off in Settings. There are no advertising or tracking SDKs.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Your subscription data, spending totals, and profiles never reach us.
      SubHelm has no developer-operated servers and no account system.
    </p>
    <p>
      To improve the app we collect <strong>anonymous usage analytics</strong> via <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com">TelemetryDeck</a>,
      a privacy-focused analytics service based in Germany (GDPR-compliant). What
      this includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Which features are used (for example "a subscription was added via scan",
        "the paywall was shown") and simple counts, plus general device
        information such as app version, iOS version, and device type.
      </li>
      <li>
        A <strong>salted, hashed identifier</strong> derived from a per-app Apple vendor
        ID, used only so repeat launches aren't counted as new users. TelemetryDeck
        cannot reverse it or link it to you, and it cannot be used to track you across
        apps.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      What it <strong>never</strong> includes: subscription names, amounts, notes,
      currencies, or any content you enter. Analytics can be disabled at any time
      with <strong>Settings → Share anonymous usage data</strong>; the app works
      identically with it off. TelemetryDeck's own policy is
      at <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/">telemetrydeck.com/privacy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On your device</strong>, in the app's local database.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>In your private iCloud database</strong> (Apple CloudKit), <em>only if</em> you
        are signed into iCloud. This is the standard mechanism Apple provides to
        sync your data across your own devices and back it up. Access is controlled by
        your Apple account; the developers have no access to it. Apple's handling of this
        data is governed by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">
          Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Network requests</h2>
    <p>
      SubHelm makes a small number of network requests. <strong>
        None of them include your subscription content or any personal data that
        identifies you.</strong>
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Brand logos</strong> — to show a logo next to a subscription, the app
        sends the brand's public website <strong>domain</strong> (for example, <code>netflix.com</code>)
        to <a href="https://logo.dev">logo.dev</a> and receives a logo image. No
        personal information is sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Currency exchange rates</strong> — to convert amounts into your preferred
        currency, the app requests reference rates from <a href="https://www.frankfurter.app">frankfurter.app</a>,
        sending only a <strong>currency code</strong> (for example, <code>GBP</code>).
        No personal information is sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Anonymous analytics</strong> — usage events are sent
        to <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com">TelemetryDeck</a> as described above,
        unless you turn analytics off in Settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>iCloud sync</strong> — handled by Apple CloudKit as described above.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      If you are offline, the app falls back gracefully (generic icons,
      last-known rates) and keeps working.
    </p>

    <h2>Receipts and the AI assistant</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Receipt scanning</strong> is performed <strong>entirely on your device</strong>.
        Receipt images are read locally to pre-fill subscription details and are never
        uploaded.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <strong>AI assistant</strong> runs <strong>on-device</strong> using Apple
        Intelligence on supported hardware. Your subscription information is not sent to
        any external AI service.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      Renewal and free-trial reminders are scheduled <strong>
        locally on your device</strong>. They are not sent through any external service.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete data:</strong> remove any subscription or profile in the app at
        any time.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Turn off analytics:</strong> Settings → Share anonymous usage data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stop iCloud sync:</strong> sign out of iCloud, or disable iCloud for
        SubHelm in the iOS Settings app.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      SubHelm is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any data
      from anyone. It is rated 4+.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date above will change. Material
      changes will be reflected in an app update.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(48px, 6vw, 84px) var(--gutter) clamp(72px, 9vw, 110px);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.2vw, 50px);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 0 0 2.4em;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 21px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 2.4em 0 0.6em;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  p {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  em {
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: inherit;
  }

  ul,
  ol {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  }

  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--band);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 1px 5px;
  }

  a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
</style>
